strings.ITA_party_unity_desc:
Italian democracy is young, and the balance of power is constantly shifting. The creation of a free Italy saw three major competitors rise up, one of them a party, and the other two uneasy coalitions.

The Fronte Democratico is made up of the Italian Socialist Party, the Italian Social Democratic Party, and a few other minor parties, as well as a small but vocal radical wing.

The Blocchi Nazionali is made up of the Italian Democratic Party of Monarchist Unity, the National Democrats and the Italian Social Movement.

Finally, the Democrazia Cristiana is split into two wings, a more liberal one and a more conservative one.

Unity updates weekly.

