strings.ITA_ENI_exploitation_desc:
Born as a small state owned oil company in the 1930s, over the decades the Ente Nazionale Idrocarburi rose to prominence under the guidance of Enrico Mattei, eventually becoming the largest oil company in the world. Entirely owned by the Italian state, ENI is today the economic cornerstone of the Italian empire, exploiting the vast oil reserves of the numerous countries in Italy's sphere. Investing into ENI is crucial to keep the oil flowing, and the Italian economy afloat - however, given the large amount of resources necessary to increase ENI operations, investments should be pondered carefully.

